            0.406,
            0.106
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "Activity 8.8: Let us explore"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.117,
            0.517,
            0.137
          ],
          "content": " Take identical caps of two bottles."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.143,
            0.655,
            0.164
          ],
          "content": " Pour equal amount of water in each of the cap."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.169,
            0.743,
            0.211
          ],
          "content": " Place one of the cap in sunlight and keep the other in shade as shown in Fig. 8.6."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.216,
            0.738,
            0.237
          ],
          "content": " Observe the two caps of bottles after every 15 minutes."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.242,
            0.743,
            0.284
          ],
          "content": " Record the time taken for the water to completely evaporate in each case."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.288,
            0.743,
            0.331
          ],
          "content": " You can also repeat this activity on a windy or a rainy day, and record your observations."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.343,
            0.74,
            0.638
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [
            {
              "bbox": [
                0.209,
                0.65,
                0.647,
                0.667
              ],
              "content": "Fig. 8.6: Evaporation of water in sunlight and in shade"
            }
          ],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_12_image_7.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.68,
            0.742,
            0.722
          ],
          "content": "What conclusions can you draw from Activity 8.8 and other similar experiences?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.727,
            0.724,
            0.769
          ],
          "content": " Water evaporates faster from the cap kept in sunlight compared to the cap kept in shade."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.774,
            0.744,
            0.877
          ],
          "content": "It is a common observation that clothes dry faster on a hot sunny day. Do clothes dry faster or slower on a windy day? It is once again a common observation that clothes dry faster on a windy day. With the increase in the movement of air, water evaporates faster."
        },
        {
          "type": "aside_text",
          "bbox": [
            0.889,
            0.697,
            0.909,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": "A Journey through States of Water"
        },
